1
00:00:00,132 --> 00:00:01,839
One Node service.

2
00:00:01,839 --> 00:00:05,473
Screen and activity signals feed a decision context;

3
00:00:05,473 --> 00:00:09,757
a hypothesis engine ranks questions by information gain;

4
00:00:09,757 --> 00:00:13,402
only a deterministic gate can authorise speech.

5
00:00:13,402 --> 00:00:20,148
Z3 and the expert's own words build the rulebook that drives the tutor and an MCP guardrail,

6
00:00:20,148 --> 00:00:22,330
all on an append-only ledger.

7
00:00:23,136 --> 00:00:30,090
The gate needs every condition: silence, an idle screen, no typing, a breakpoint,

8
00:00:30,090 --> 00:00:32,854
a valuable question, and budget.

9
00:00:32,854 --> 00:00:38,299
In the first live runs it decided within 3 milliseconds at the 95th percentile;

10
00:00:38,299 --> 00:00:44,115
in the re-run, 23 of 26 decisions met the 250 millisecond bound,

11
00:00:44,115 --> 00:00:47,517
and three waited behind slow production round trips.

12
00:00:48,607 --> 00:00:52,763
The voice agent's brain is our thin custom LLM.

13
00:00:52,763 --> 00:00:57,071
Real requests to this build: no credentials, rejected.

14
00:00:57,071 --> 00:01:00,054
No authorisation, skip turn.

15
00:01:00,054 --> 00:01:03,874
A valid one-time nonce, the exact question.

16
00:01:03,874 --> 00:01:06,695
The same nonce again, skip turn.

17
00:01:06,695 --> 00:01:11,827
On production, an unauthorised turn stayed silent for 8 seconds.

18
00:01:13,216 --> 00:01:19,009
Z3 checks the confirmed rules within the domain constraints and returns witnesses:

19
00:01:19,009 --> 00:01:23,502
undecided cases, real conflicts, and thresholds.

20
00:01:23,502 --> 00:01:27,194
Coverage closes only when all four criteria hold.

21
00:01:28,910 --> 00:01:33,600
A confirmed rule must cite an exact quote and a real frame.

22
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:37,548
The trace walks the ledger from pixels to rule.

23
00:01:39,288 --> 00:01:43,247
Live runs found a stall: a health check waited 10.

24
00:01:43,247 --> 00:01:45,244
5 seconds and 5.

25
00:01:45,244 --> 00:01:46,695
3 seconds.

26
00:01:46,695 --> 00:01:49,377
Heavy work now runs in worker threads,

27
00:01:49,377 --> 00:01:53,452
and production's event-loop delay at p99 is 1.

28
00:01:53,452 --> 00:01:54,996
8 milliseconds.

29
00:01:54,996 --> 00:01:56,111
But one 13.

30
00:01:56,111 --> 00:02:01,486
9 seconds host-level freeze remains, and its mitigations are not yet verified.

31
00:02:02,819 --> 00:02:08,833
Apprentice-Bench is deterministic: a hidden-policy program stands in for the expert.

32
00:02:08,833 --> 00:02:12,943
8 targeted questions cut unsafe approvals from 14.

33
00:02:12,943 --> 00:02:14,661
9 percent to 1.

34
00:02:14,661 --> 00:02:15,590
2 percent.

35
00:02:16,580 --> 00:02:21,503
And every demo can fall back to a verified replay of a real run.

36
00:02:21,503 --> 00:02:24,289
Change one byte, and it refuses to play.

37
00:02:26,038 --> 00:02:27,489
LLMs infer.

38
00:02:27,489 --> 00:02:28,871
Experts confirm.

39
00:02:28,871 --> 00:02:30,171
Code enforces.

